                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      the latest com.puppycrawl.tools.checkstyle have dependency like<br/>
&lt;dependency&gt;<br/>
      &lt;groupId&gt;com.sun&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifactId&gt;tools&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
      &lt;version&gt;1.5.0&lt;/version&gt;<br/>
      &lt;scope&gt;system&lt;/scope&gt;<br/>
      &lt;systemPath&gt;${java.home}/../lib/tools.jar&lt;/systemPath&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
but on Mac OSX, there&#39;s no tools.jar, it should be ${java.home}/../Classes/classes.jar instead, we need add a profile for mac to replace the path tomake the build pass.
