                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      CXF has its own UsernameToken which is used by AbstractUsernameTokenInterceptor sub-classes to populate the subject without dealing with WSS4J and making sure it works with policy-first cases along the line.<br/>
<br/>
Having CXF X509Token can make it straightforward for users to do the authentication and authorization in CXF with X509 certs and make it a common knowledge. Additionally a JAASLoginInterceptor should also be enhanced to handle X509 related callbacks.
  </td>
