                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
If the wsdl defines a policy for a fault only, like:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
           &lt;wsdl:fault name=&quot;DoubleItFault&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;wsp:PolicyReference URI=&quot;#SignedOnlyMsgPolicy&quot; /&gt;<br/>
                &lt;soap:body use=&quot;literal&quot; name=&quot;DoubleItFault&quot; /&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/wsdl:fault&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
the policy is not being applied if the implementation has the operation unwrapped (the default).   If the operation is BARE, then the policy is applied correctly.<br/>

  </td>
