                <tr id="issuerow12496213" rel="12496213" data-issuekey="CXF-3260" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3260" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3260">CXF-3260</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JAX-RS: org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.utils.Messages properties file missing definition for NO_CRI_MATCH
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Glen Mazza
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ka-Lok Fung
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ka-Lok Fung
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 21/Jan/11 02:24 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 18/Apr/11 12:44 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 21/Jan/11 05:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.3.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.4            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">300</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">300</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Java 1.6<br/>
CXF 2.3.1 / CXF 2.3.2
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      JAXRSUtils.selectResourceClass expects a message keyed by &quot;NO_CRI_MATCH&quot;. However, when you look in the Messages properties file (org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.utils.Messages), it is absent.<br/>
<br/>
Because this message is absent, the Java runtime needlessly generates a ResourceNotFound exception for every resource in your application that it examined and couldn&#39;t match the incoming method.<br/>
<br/>
The suggested fix, is of course, to define that string. Here&#39;s what I came up with:<br/>
<br/>
NO_CRI_MATCH=Resource class {1} will not be selected, request path : {0}
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     0%
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     0%
</td>
