                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Given the following method<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
 @WebMethod<br/>
    public BaseResponse removeDepositLimits(<br/>
            @WebParam( name = SERVICE_AUTH ) @XmlElement( required = true ) final Authorisation auth ,<br/>
            @WebParam( name = TOKEN ) @XmlElement( required = true ) final String token ,<br/>
            @WebParam( name = &quot;timeFrame&quot; ) @XmlElement( required = true ) final DepositLimit.TimeFrame timeFrame )<br/>
{code}<br/>
when timeFrame is a value that&#39;s not in the TimeFrame enum, timeFrame is set to null, this should return an error to the invoker instead.<br/>

