                <tr id="issuerow12498119" rel="12498119" data-issuekey="CXF-3320" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3320" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3320">CXF-3320</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                wsdl2js generated code fails to parse a Java Map&lt;String, String&gt; property
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Robbie Gieze
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Robbie Gieze
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 09/Feb/11 13:06 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Nov/13 21:50 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.4,                     2.2.12,                     2.3.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Aegis Databinding,                     JavaScript Client            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP SP3 Pro English, JDK 1.6.0.20, Aegis, CXF on server side is 2.2.4
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m using Apache CXF to expose a Java object through SOAP which has the following property:<br/>
<br/>
private Map&lt;String,String&gt; constraintParams;<br/>
<br/>
This gives me a correct WSDL file and I can use the SOAP method with no problems from tools like soapUI.<br/>
<br/>
But I want to use the SOAP service from javascript. So I use the wsdl2js tool of CXF and it generates a .js file. When I use the javascript file it fails to parse the SOAP response from the server. <br/>
<br/>
The SOAP XML part that the javascript code fails to deserialize looks like this:<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;ns3:constraintParams&gt;<br/>
    &lt;ns1:entry&gt;<br/>
      &lt;ns1:key&gt;regex&lt;/ns1:key&gt;<br/>
      &lt;ns1:value&gt;^.+$&lt;/ns1:value&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/ns1:entry&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/ns3:constraintParams&gt;<br/>
<br/>
It seems like the generated js code tries to deserialize the &lt;entry&gt; tag but the wsdl2js generator didn&#39;t actually generate that function, so the code of the generator is calling a function that it didn&#39;t generate. The following line in the js gives a &quot;services_systemcontrol_mydomain_com__entry_deserialize&quot; is not defined&quot; error.<br/>
<br/>
   arrayItem = services_systemcontrol_mydomain_com__entry_deserialize(cxfjsutils, curElement);<br/>
<br/>
At this moment the curElement property has the &lt;entry&gt; tag but the deserialize function simply is not in the generated js file.<br/>
<br/>
Do I do anything wrong or is there another way that does work that I could look into?<br/>
<br/>
On the server side I&#39;m using 2.2.4, I tested the wsdl2js tool of versions 2.2.4, 2.2.12, 2.3.2 the result is always as above. I&#39;m also using aegis<br/>

  </td>
