</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 64Bit Jboss5.1 cxf 2.3.4
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      We have multiple war files exposing different endpoints. We use Wss4J Interceptor which in turn calls SAAJInInterceptor.<br/>
When only one War is running everything works fine. When both are running and you call a service on the first war it works. when you call it on the second War it hangs on MessageFactory.newInstance(....); in the SAAJ interceptor<br/>
Which eventually leads to a out of memory exception.<br/>

  </td>
