                <tr id="issuerow12506869" rel="12506869" data-issuekey="CXF-3510" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3510" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3510">CXF-3510</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                wrong destination determination by OSGi based CXF entry point (regarding its fallback logic)
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Akitoshi Yoshida
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Akitoshi Yoshida
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Akitoshi Yoshida
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/May/11 16:00 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Aug/11 14:43 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 23/May/11 14:28 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4,                     2.3.4            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.4.1,                     2.3.5            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">7200</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">7200</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-3559                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      This problem is described in cxf-user thread<br/>
<br/>
http://cxf.547215.n5.nabble.com/strange-destination-determination-logic-used-by-the-osgi-based-cxf-entry-point-td4385312.html<br/>
<br/>
In summary, the http entry point in the OSGi container uses the destination determination logic using a simple request path matching when there is no exact match of the request URL path to one of the registered destination paths. Consequently, when you have a service registered at &quot;/abc&quot;, a request to any URL path starting with this string, for example, &quot;/abc2&quot;, &quot;/abctest&quot; is also fowarded to this service. And this is not intended.<br/>
<br/>
The intention of this fallback logic was for the rest based calls to forward a request with an additional path argument to its correct service. For examples, requests to &quot;/abc/def&quot; or &quot;/abc/1/2&quot; should be forwarded to the service registered at &quot;/abc&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ll be suggesting the change required in org.apache.cxf.transport.http_osgi.OsgiServletController for 2.3.x and org.apache.cxf.transport.http.DestinationRegistryImpl for 2.4.x.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
