                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have a request scoped resource via a RequestScopeResourceFactory and &lt;aop:scoped-proxy /&gt; as described on http://cxf.apache.org/docs/jaxrs-services-configuration.html#JAXRSServicesConfiguration-Lifecyclemanagement to be able to inject @PathParams on class fields. This works as expected however the mapped parameters do not show up in the auto-generated WADL. After a quick look in the source code of org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.model.wadl.WADLGenerator it seems it is only looking for method-level parameters.<br/>
<br/>

