                <tr id="issuerow12512966" rel="12512966" data-issuekey="CXF-3633" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3633" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3633">CXF-3633</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Provide a way of disabling sending an AppliesTo element when requesting a security token via the STSClient
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 06/Jul/11 11:28 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Aug/11 03:29 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 06/Jul/11 11:36 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.4.2,                     2.5            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
When requesting a security token via the STSClient, the address to be sent in the AppliesTo element is passed through to the requestSecurityToken method as a String. It can accept a null string, in which case the AppliesTo element is not sent. However, when used with the IssuedTokenInterceptorProvider, it falls back to the endpoint address at all times, and so it is not possible to disable sending the AppliesTo element. This task is to add a boolean property to the STSClient to disable sending an AppliesTo element.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310060"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310220"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312322"></td>
