</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The current CXF Slf4jLogger just invokes the internal slf4j logger object. <br/>
In this way, it cannot show the original logging location.<br/>
For example, when logging configuration contains something like &#39;%C:%L&#39;, it <br/>
prints the Slf4jLogger class name and its line number instead of the caller&#39;s class name and its line number.<br/>
In order to show the original logging locations nicely, we can use LocationAwareLogger#log(, fqcn, ...) operation. With provision of the FQCN of the wrapper class, the underlying slf4j logger will find the exact logging location.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ll provide a patch for this in this issue.
  </td>
