                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;ve found a piece of incorrect code in org.apache.cxf.transport.servlet.BaseUrlHelper method getBaseURL()<br/>
There&#39;s such a code at line 41: &quot;index = reqPrefix.indexOf(basePath);&quot;<br/>
This code handles URL badly when host name starts with application context name.<br/>
<br/>
Example:<br/>
URL &quot;http://arm.mycompany.com:8998/arm/arm&quot; will produce return value of &quot;http://arm&quot; instead of &quot;http://arm.mycompany.com:8998/arm&quot;
  </td>
