                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      rt/rs/security/xml module should host the code to do with XML security: signature and encryption.<br/>
<br/>
it may also host SAML related code simply because SAML assertions are in XML format and they can have XML signatures and<br/>
in principle - encrypted as part of XML payload.<br/>
<br/>
the idea of using rt/rs/security/*xml* is also about adding in due time support for non-XML security, ex, smime, some OAuth and OpendId helpers, Salmon (?), CAS, etc - the list is quite open ended<br/>

  </td>
