                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      CXF 2.4.1 comes with the following Jetty jars:<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
05/26/2011  08:41 AM            20,083 jetty-continuation-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
05/26/2011  08:40 AM           108,833 jetty-http-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
05/26/2011  08:40 AM            89,024 jetty-io-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
05/26/2011  08:45 AM            83,096 jetty-security-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
05/26/2011  08:44 AM           294,399 jetty-server-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
05/26/2011  08:39 AM           207,534 jetty-util-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
How about using the all-in-one jar instead?<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
05/26/2011  09:02 AM         1,572,841 jetty-all-7.4.2.v20110526.jar<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
It&#39;s another ~800 KB (all the CXF jars are already ~30MB) but would make life easier for those of use that embed CXF in Jetty so we can use all the Jetty bells and whistles.<br/>

  </td>
