                <tr id="issuerow12519213" rel="12519213" data-issuekey="CXF-3748" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3748" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3748">CXF-3748</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Using Dispatch API with SOAPMessage type fails to set WS-Addressing action header properly if there&#39;s whitespace after the soap:body
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jesse Pangburn
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jesse Pangburn
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Aug/11 00:02 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 06/Sep/11 20:49 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 19/Aug/11 02:08 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3.7,                     2.4.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">7200</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">7200</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      if you use a SOAPMessage instead of a Source then the following function fails (ignoring the exception) and your ws-addressing action doesn&#39;t get set- if you have any whitespace after the soap:body element before your first payload element:<br/>
    private String getPayloadElementName(SOAPMessage soapMessage) {<br/>
        try {            <br/>
            SOAPElement element  = (SOAPElement)soapMessage.getSOAPBody().getChildElements().next();<br/>
            return new QName(element.getNamespaceURI(), element.getLocalName()).toString();<br/>
        } catch (Exception e) {<br/>
            //ignore<br/>
        }<br/>
        return null;<br/>
        <br/>
    }<br/>
<br/>
This fails because the .next() call at the end gets a text node instead of an element object so the cast fails.  So inexplicably your ws-addressing action header doesn&#39;t get set as far as the user sees.
  </td>
