                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m wondering if all of the instances of silenced exceptions in the example projects really need to be silenced.<br/>
<br/>
Note: &quot;Don&#39;t silently ignore exceptions, except in those few cases where you can&#39;t do anything anyway.&quot; -- http://leepoint.net/notes-java/principles_and_practices/style/style-practices-summary.html<br/>
<br/>
What I&#39;m implying is that [ex].printStackTrace() or [ex].getMessage() should be applied where appropriate.<br/>
