                <tr id="issuerow12530543" rel="12530543" data-issuekey="CXF-3895" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3895" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3895">CXF-3895</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                add support for Jetty&#39;s password obfuscation methods
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Michael Heß
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Michael Heß
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 07/Nov/11 09:22 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Dec/11 16:15 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 08/Dec/11 22:00 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.5.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Configuration            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Java 6<br/>
Windows XP SP3<br/>
CXF 2.4.2
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      For SSL connectors, the Jetty configuration allows definition of keystore and truststore passwords in a obfuscated fashion. See http://wiki.eclipse.org/Jetty/Howto/Secure_Passwords for details. Currently this does not work when using the Spring based configuration for jetty, i.e. using for example this<br/>
<br/>
&lt;sec:keyStore type=&quot;JKS&quot; password=&quot;OBF:1sot1v961saj1v9i1v941sar1v9g1sox&quot; file=&quot;conf/keystore&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
will lead to an exception on startup, which is identical to those that come up when an invalid keystore password is provided.<br/>
<br/>
My guess is, that the &quot;OBF:&quot; prefix is not detected by the configuration hook, and therefore the provided password string is used as-is. (But I am just guessing here...)
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    configuration, cxf, jetty, keys, password, security</td>
