</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      With CXF 2.4.3 working on Java first web services (attached Eclipse project CXF-WSDLTest.zip) produces the following error when attempting to generate WSDL with referenced XSD files.<br/>
<br/>
SEVERE: Schema element {urn:example.com:fault1}appFault references undefined type {urn:example.com:fault}appFaultDetails for service {urn:example.com:role1}RoleApiService.<br/>
<br/>
I want/need to do this, because several services do share the Fault, FaultDetails and error code beans.<br/>
<br/>
Here are my questions:<br/>
* Why is java2ws not seeing the appFaultDetails (generating the severe message above)?<br/>
* Why is java2ws not generating the import statement for the fault.xsd?<br/>
* Why is the import statement for the role.xsd not using the stated location from the package-info.java file?<br/>
<br/>

