                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-3929                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Tokens passed in OnBehalfOf element are not validated. It&#39;s the responsibility of the TokenProvider implementation to validate that.<br/>
<br/>
A proposal has been discussed here:<br/>
http://cxf.547215.n5.nabble.com/STS-OnBehalfOf-token-validation-SAMLTokenProvider-td5003544.html<br/>
<br/>
OnBehalfOf token validation is moved to the TokenIssueOperation and the ReceivedToken is enhanced with the following attributes:<br/>
- was it a token of ws-security header (like ReceivedToken), onbehalfof, actas<br/>
- successfully validated (it could be a token which depends on other constraints to be fully accepted)<br/>
- original DOM element<br/>
- transformed DOM element (used if the token is passed by ref, also supported by SAML spec)<br/>
- principal (mostly, you only need the principal to issue a new token)<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
