                <tr id="issuerow12539507" rel="12539507" data-issuekey="CXF-4056" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4056" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4056">CXF-4056</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Faults on server are echoing headers back to the client
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Jan/12 18:36 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Apr/12 16:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 23/Jan/12 20:27 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.5.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3.10,                     2.4.7,                     2.5.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The SoapHeaderOutFilterInterceptor that filters out the incoming headers is only installed on the Out chain.  It&#39;s not installed on the OutFault chain.  Thus, all the incoming headers are echoed back to the client which could result in WS-Addressing issues, security issues, etc...
